#: ../../hydrogen_chain/band_formation.rst:55
msgid ""
"原子数依存性の計算には密度フィッティング（DF）SCFを、後半のスピン制限解・非制限解の比較と安定性解析には近似のない4中心積分（PK法）を使いました。\\"
" PBEの積分グリッドはPsi4の既定値です。以下に示す数値はすべて収束したSCF解から取得しています。"
msgstr ""
"We used density-fitted (DF) SCF to study the dependence on atom count. "
"For the later comparison of spin-restricted and spin-unrestricted "
"solutions and for the stability analysis, we used exact four-center "
"integrals (the PK method). \\ The PBE integration grid was the Psi4 "
"default. All values shown below come from converged SCF solutions."

#: ../../hydrogen_chain/band_formation.rst:61
msgid "Tight-Binding 模型による予想"
msgstr "Prediction from the Tight-Binding Model"

#: ../../hydrogen_chain/band_formation.rst:63
msgid ""
"孤立した水素原子の基底状態では、電子が1s軌道を占めます。\\ "
"水素原子を2個近づけると、2つの1s軌道から結合性軌道と反結合性軌道ができます。\\ さらに原子を増やすと、 :math:`N` "
"個の1s基底関数から :math:`N` 個の分子軌道ができます。"
msgstr ""
"In the ground state of an isolated hydrogen atom, the electron occupies a"
" 1s orbital. \\ When two hydrogen atoms approach each other, their two 1s"
" orbitals form a bonding orbital and an antibonding orbital. \\ As more "
"atoms are added, :math:`N` 1s basis functions form :math:`N` molecular "
"orbitals."

#: ../../hydrogen_chain/band_formation.rst:67
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"中性の :math:`\\mathrm{H}_N` 鎖には :math:`N` 個の電子があり、スピン制限の閉殻計算では、エネルギーの低い "
":math:`N/2` 個の分子軌道を2電子ずつ占有します。1原子あたり1電子なので、1軌道のバンド模型でいえば **半充填** の状態です。"
msgstr ""
"A neutral :math:`\\mathrm{H}_N` chain has :math:`N` electrons. In a spin-"
"restricted closed-shell calculation, two electrons occupy each of the "
":math:`N/2` lowest-energy molecular orbitals. With one electron per atom,"
" a one-orbital band model is at **half filling**."

#: ../../hydrogen_chain/band_formation.rst:69
msgid ""
"この状況を説明する最も簡単なモデルが、隣接原子間のホッピングだけを考える強束縛（tight-binding）模型です。\\ "
"各原子の軌道エネルギーを :math:`\\varepsilon_0` 、隣接原子間のホッピングを :math:`t` とすると、開放端の "
":math:`N` 原子鎖の固有値は"
msgstr ""
"The simplest model for this situation is a tight-binding model with "
"hopping only between neighboring atoms. \\ If each atom has orbital "
"energy :math:`\\varepsilon_0` and the hopping between neighboring atoms "
"is :math:`t`, the eigenvalues of an open-ended chain of :math:`N` atoms "
"are"

#: ../../hydrogen_chain/band_formation.rst:72
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"E_j = \\varepsilon_0 - 2t\\cos\\left(\\frac{j\\pi}{N+1}\\right),\n"
"\\qquad j = 1, \\ldots, N"
msgstr ""
"E_j = \\varepsilon_0 - 2t\\cos\\left(\\frac{j\\pi}{N+1}\\right),\n"
"\\qquad j = 1, \\ldots, N"

#: ../../hydrogen_chain/band_formation.rst:77
msgid "となります。一方、原子間隔 :math:`a` の無限周期鎖のバンド分散は"
msgstr ""
"whereas the band dispersion of an infinite periodic chain with "
"interatomic spacing :math:`a` is"

#: ../../hydrogen_chain/band_formation.rst:79
msgid "E(k) = \\varepsilon_0 - 2t\\cos(ka)"
msgstr "E(k) = \\varepsilon_0 - 2t\\cos(ka)"

#: ../../hydrogen_chain/band_formation.rst:84
msgid ""
"です。有限鎖の :math:`j` 番目の準位に形式的に :math:`k_j a = j\\pi/(N+1)` という **擬似波数** "
"を割り当てると、\\ 原子数を増やすほど、このコサインカーブを細かくサンプリングしていくことが分かります。"
msgstr ""
"If we formally assign the :math:`j`-th level of the finite chain the "
"value :math:`k_j a = j\\pi/(N+1)` as its **pseudo wave number**, \\ "
"increasing the number of atoms samples this cosine curve more finely."

#: ../../hydrogen_chain/band_formation.rst:88
msgid "分子軌道エネルギーがバンドになるか"
msgstr "Do Molecular Orbital Energies Form a Band?"

#: ../../hydrogen_chain/band_formation.rst:90
msgid ""
"RKS-PBE計算で得た分子軌道エネルギーを、上記の擬似波数に対して並べたのが :numref:`fig-hchain-pbe-levels` "
"です。"
msgstr ""
":numref:`fig-hchain-pbe-levels` plots the molecular orbital energies "
"obtained from the RKS-PBE calculations against the pseudo wave number "
"defined above."

#: ../../hydrogen_chain/band_formation.rst:96
msgid ""
"RKS-PBEで求めた分子軌道エネルギー（原子数ごとに軌道エネルギーの平均を差し引いています）。黒い破線は、式 :eq:`nntb-band` で"
" :math:`t \\simeq 1.87` eV とした場合（後述）のバンドです。\\ 横軸は擬似波数 :math:`ka = "
"j\\pi/(N+1)` 、中央にある垂直な点線は半充填位置（電子占有／非占有の境界） :math:`ka = \\pi/2` を示しています。"
msgstr ""
"These are the RKS-PBE molecular orbital energies relative to the chain "
"mean for each atom count. The black dashed line is the band given by "
"Equation :eq:`nntb-band` with :math:`t \\simeq 1.87` eV, as explained "
"below. \\ The horizontal axis shows the assigned pseudo wave number "
":math:`ka = j\\pi/(N+1)`, and the vertical dotted line at the center "
"marks half filling at :math:`ka = \\pi/2`, the boundary between occupied "
"and unoccupied levels."

#: ../../hydrogen_chain/band_formation.rst:99
msgid ""
"原子数が少ないうちは準位がまばらですが、 :math:`N` = 32、64になると点が1本の滑らかな曲線を描きます。\\ "
"たしかに、分子軌道の集まりからバンド状のエネルギースペクトルが生まれる様子が、\\ 数値実験として直接確認できました。"
msgstr ""
"For small numbers of atoms, the levels are sparse, but at :math:`N` = 32 "
"and 64 the points trace a smooth curve. \\ This numerical experiment "
"indeed shows directly how a band-like energy spectrum \\ emerges from a "
"collection of molecular orbitals."

#: ../../hydrogen_chain/band_formation.rst:103
msgid ""
"ただし、ここで計算しているのは、あくまでも有限の孤立分子であり、周期結晶のバンド構造そのものではありません。\\ "
"擬似波数が実際の波動関数の空間振動と対応しているかは、軌道係数を解析して検証する必要があります。\\ RKS-"
"PBEの準位は黒い破線に近いものの、特に上下端付近ではずれています。"
msgstr ""
"However, the calculation is only for a finite, isolated molecule and does"
" not give the band structure of a periodic crystal itself. \\ Verifying "
"whether the pseudo wave number corresponds to the actual spatial "
"oscillations of the wave function requires an analysis of the orbital "
"coefficients. \\ The RKS-PBE levels lie close to the black dashed line "
"but deviate from it, especially near the upper and lower ends."

#: ../../hydrogen_chain/band_formation.rst:107
msgid ""
"例えば :math:`N` = 64の全軌道エネルギーに :math:`A+B\\cos(ka)` を最小二乗フィットすると、\\ "
"二乗平均平方根誤差は約 0.312 eV になります。\\ :math:`C\\cos(2ka)` を加えて、フィッティングの自由度を上げると、約"
" 0.041 eV まで減らせます。\\ "
"これは、最近接以遠の相互作用、軌道の重なり、自己無撞着ポテンシャルなどが、単純な模型との差に寄与しているためだと考えられますが、\\ "
"ここでは、これ以上は立ち入りません。"
msgstr ""
"For example, for :math:`N` = 64 a least-squares fit of "
":math:`A+B\\cos(ka)` to all orbital energies \\ gives a root mean square "
"error of about 0.312 eV. With \\ :math:`C\\cos(2ka)` added to make the "
"fit more flexible, the error drops to about 0.041 eV. \\ Interactions "
"beyond nearest neighbors, orbital overlap, and the self-consistent "
"potential are among the likely contributors to the difference from the "
"simple model, but \\ we do not investigate those contributions further "
"here."

#: ../../hydrogen_chain/band_formation.rst:114
msgid "RHFの場合"
msgstr "RHF Results"

#: ../../hydrogen_chain/band_formation.rst:116
msgid ""
"同じ水素鎖の計算を、今度はRHF法で行い、先ほどと同様に、\\ 原子数を変えて軌道エネルギーをプロットしてみると :numref:`fig-"
"hchain-rhf-levels` のようになります。\\ RKS-"
"PBEの場合とは大きく様子が異なり、はっきりとバンドギャップが現れているのがわかります。"
msgstr ""
"We ran RHF calculations on the same hydrogen chains and, as before, \\ "
"plotted the orbital energies for different atom counts in :numref:`fig-"
"hchain-rhf-levels`. \\ The RHF plot differs markedly from the RKS-PBE "
"plot in that it shows a clearly visible band gap."

#: ../../hydrogen_chain/band_formation.rst:124
msgid ""
"RHFで求めた分子軌道エネルギー。軸の定義と黒い破線は :numref:`fig-hchain-pbe-levels` "
"と同じです。破線はPBEのギャップから求めた :math:`t \\simeq 1.87` "
"eVの強束縛模型を比較の基準として示しており、RHFへのフィットではありません。縦軸の表示範囲はRHFの準位に合わせています。"
msgstr ""
"These are the RHF molecular orbital energies. The axes and the black "
"dashed line are defined as in :numref:`fig-hchain-pbe-levels`. The dashed"
" line is the tight-binding model with :math:`t \\simeq 1.87` eV obtained "
"from the PBE gap, shown as a reference for comparison; it is not a fit to"
" the RHF results. The vertical range is chosen to show the RHF levels."

#: ../../hydrogen_chain/band_formation.rst:126
msgid ""
":numref:`tab-hchain-gaps` および :numref:`fig-hchain-gaps` に、RHFおよびRKS-"
"PBEによる、\\ 最高被占有軌道（HOMO）と最低空軌道（LUMO）のエネルギー差（HOMO-"
"LUMOギャップ）の、水素鎖長に対する変化を示しています。\\ これをみると、RKS-PBEの場合は、水素鎖長とともに HOMO-LUMO "
"ギャップがどんどん小さくなっていくのに対し、\\ RHFの場合は、調べた鎖長の範囲では大きな軌道ギャップが残ることが分かります。\\ "
"その結果、RHF法で水素鎖のバンドを描くと、\\ :numref:`fig-hchain-rhf-levels` "
"のようにバンドギャップが現れることになります。"
msgstr ""
":numref:`tab-hchain-gaps` and :numref:`fig-hchain-gaps` compare how the "
"RHF and RKS-PBE HOMO–LUMO gaps, \\ the energy differences between the "
"highest occupied molecular orbital (HOMO) and the lowest unoccupied "
"molecular orbital (LUMO), change with hydrogen chain length. \\ The RKS-"
"PBE HOMO–LUMO gap shrinks rapidly as the chain length increases, whereas "
"\\ a large orbital gap persists in RHF over the chain lengths studied. \\"
" As a result, the RHF band plot for the hydrogen chain shows a band gap, "
"as in \\ :numref:`fig-hchain-rhf-levels`."

